{"name":"Blue Ruin","hex":"#0066dd","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"blue ruin","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Low-end gin, usually home-made.","Complete and utter ruin, desolation."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue_ruin"}],"entries":[{"title":"Blue Ruin","blocks":[{"text":"Blue Ruin is a 2013 American independent Southern Gothic revenge thriller film written and directed by Jeremy Saulnier, and starring Macon Blair. Saulnier funded production on the film through a successful Kickstarter campaign, which MTV called \"the perfect example of what crowdfunding can accomplish.\""}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/9/9f/Blue_Ruin_film_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue_Ruin","wikidata":"Q13380375"},{"title":"Blue Ruin (band)","blocks":[{"text":"Blue Ruin were an Australian blues rock band, which started as Scrap Museum in 1984. Their third studio album, I'm Gonna Smile, was nominated for Best Independent Release at the ARIA Music Awards of 1991. The group had released three other studio albums, Such Sweet Thunder, Flame and Tattoo Tears (1993), before disbanding in 1995. Mainstay members were Ian \"Quincy\" McLean on lead vocals and Mulaim Vela on lead guitar."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue_Ruin_(band)","wikidata":"Q28421795"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue","wikidata":"Q1088"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/9/9f/Blue_Ruin_film_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/9/9f/Blue_Ruin_film_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABlue_Ruin_film_poster.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Q%26_A%2C_%22Blue_Ruin%22_Fantastic_Fest_with_Writer-Director_Jeremy_Saulnier_and_lead_actor_Macon_Blair_%2810620655425%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Q%26_A%2C_%22Blue_Ruin%22_Fantastic_Fest_with_Writer-Director_Jeremy_Saulnier_and_lead_actor_Macon_Blair_%2810620655425%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Q%26_A%2C_%22Blue_Ruin%22_Fantastic_Fest_with_Writer-Director_Jeremy_Saulnier_and_lead_actor_Macon_Blair_%2810620655425%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/1280px-Q%26_A%2C_%22Blue_Ruin%22_Fantastic_Fest_with_Writer-Director_Jeremy_Saulnier_and_lead_actor_Macon_Blair_%2810620655425%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Q%26_A%2C_%22Blue_Ruin%22_Fantastic_Fest_with_Writer-Director_Jeremy_Saulnier_and_lead_actor_Macon_Blair_%2810620655425%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Q%26_A%2C_%22Blue_Ruin%22_Fantastic_Fest_with_Writer-Director_Jeremy_Saulnier_and_lead_actor_Macon_Blair_%2810620655425%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_camp